A||||4||GTMike||where is the oil pressure sending unit in 2.8???||||1||
Z||000000||GTMike||12-16-2001||02:32 PM||||i need to locate this so i can replace it  where is it on the engine???? <P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||12-16-2001||02:41 PM||||look between the battery and the engine block and right behind the EGR solenoid. You will see a cylindrical object with a three wire connector on top. That's the Oil Pressure Sending Unit. Use a 15mm open end wrench on the bottom of the unit to remove it.<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||12-16-2001||03:01 PM||||thanks i thougtthta was it but the one i got to replace it only has 2 prongs  not 3.  do you think it will still work?  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||12-16-2001||03:18 PM||||no. You need one for an '85-'87 2.8L V-6.||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||12-16-2001||04:02 PM||||You can see it in this picture. Just follow the line from the oil filter up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero17.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
